  "description": "Like bacon, sliced Canadian bacon is not one of the meats you'd think would benefit from being cooked sous vide. But as it turns out, sous-vide ham is revelatory: Cooked low and slow overnight, it retains all of its juiciness, but gains an incredibly luxurious, buttery-soft tenderness as its connective tissue and muscles break down.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: Canadian bacon → ham; vegetable oil → canola oil\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Cooked, unseared ham can be refrigerated for up to 1 week, or frozen for up to several months. If frozen, transfer to refrigerator and allow to thaw overnight before searing.",
